  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Age and disability inclusive humanitarian response for earthquake affected population of Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1: The wellbeing and independence of 375 Person with Disability (PWD) in the target locations have improved after the provision of Assistive Products.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this fund, HAI and the local partner, the Syrian Expatriate Medical Association (SEMA), will support the provision of Assistive Products (AP) to older women and men, and women and men with disabilities affected by the earthquake in NWS. SEMA&apos;s protection team will identify cases with special concerns and needs and document them. These cases will be provided with assistive products such as wheelchairs, artificial limbs, walking aids, toilet chairs, incontinence products which are essential health products that must be available alongside medicines and other medical supplies to ensure comprehensive health care for people injured and/or displaced as a result of the earthquake.</narrative>
  </description>
